						<meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image">
					<meta name="Description" content="A strange change from GB is the frequency of the AI wingman's callouts to you in mission. Sure, 'Bauke Bauke' is burnt into my brain, and supposedly the new voice system should keep callouts more helpful. But its the volume of callouts thats gone down, and the game is worse for it. I was flying my MiG-15 career, and got into a furball with Sabers. At no time did the AI give me a 'bandits, four low' or even a 'Tally!' or whatever the North Korean/Russian equivalent is.">
			
	<meta name="twitter:site" content="@steam" />

						<meta property="og:title" content="AI pilot call outs :: Korea. IL-2 Series General Discussions">
					<meta property="twitter:title" content="AI pilot call outs :: Korea. IL-2 Series General Discussions">
					<meta property="og:type" content="website">
					<meta property="fb:app_id" content="105386699540688">
					<meta property="og:description" content="A strange change from GB is the frequency of the AI wingman's callouts to you in mission. Sure, 'Bauke Bauke' is burnt into my brain, and supposedly the new voice system should keep callouts more helpful. But its the volume of callouts thats gone down, and the game is worse for it. I was flying my MiG-15 career, and got into a furball with Sabers. At no time did the AI give me a 'bandits, four low' or even a 'Tally!' or whatever the North Korean/Russian equivalent is.">
					<meta property="twitter:description" content="A strange change from GB is the frequency of the AI wingman's callouts to you in mission. Sure, 'Bauke Bauke' is burnt into my brain, and supposedly the new voice system should keep callouts more helpful. But its the volume of callouts thats gone down, and the game is worse for it. I was flying my MiG-15 career, and got into a furball with Sabers. At no time did the AI give me a 'bandits, four low' or even a 'Tally!' or whatever the North Korean/Russian equivalent is.">
			
	
