					</div>
				</div>

				
				<div class="commentthread_comment_actions" >
														<a class="forum_comment_action forum_comment_action_trigger" data-tooltip-type="selector" data-tooltip-content="#forum_comment_actions_menu_573805391546343319">
					<span><i class="ico16 arrow_down"></i></span>
				</a>
			
			<div class="forum_comment_action_menu" style="display: none;" id="forum_comment_actions_menu_573805391546343319">				<a class="forum_comment_action report tooltip" href="javascript:Forum_ShowReportDialog( '103582791475538230', '766312101614724073', '573805391546193767', '49486240', '573805391546343319' );" data-tooltip-text="Report this post for inappropriate content.  Reported post are flagged for review by moderators.">
				<span class="non_breaking_space">&nbsp;</span><img src="https://community.akamai.steamstatic.com/public/images/skin_1/notification_icon_flag_dark.png?v=1">Report this post</a>
			</div>
							</div>
			</div>
			<div class="commentthread_comment_text" id="comment_content_573805391546343319">
				The Ai behavior is set on automatic by default and act on everything without requiring your flight lead input. This also means that they often won't respond to your commands.   <br>If you would rather they obey to your commands, mostly, go to settings/game/artificial intelligence and select the option &quot;Maintain Formation&quot;.  I noticed more radio replies when this is turned on, such as flight formation confirmations.<br><br>I also would like having more control on radio volume in the future.<br>My biggest negative on this topic is the often uncomprehensible ai voices forcing me to open my map screen to read the chat bubbles. <br><br>I read that a voice rework is in the works so we can expect things to get better.<br>Fly safe!			</div>
			<div class="comment_footer_ctn">
									<div></div>
				
				
									<div class="forum_comment_permlink">
						<span class="forum_comment_moderate">
													</span>
