				<div class="commentthread_comment_actions" >
														<a class="forum_comment_action forum_comment_action_trigger" data-tooltip-type="selector" data-tooltip-content="#forum_comment_actions_menu_573805391546415335">
					<span><i class="ico16 arrow_down"></i></span>
				</a>
			
			<div class="forum_comment_action_menu" style="display: none;" id="forum_comment_actions_menu_573805391546415335">				<a class="forum_comment_action report tooltip" href="javascript:Forum_ShowReportDialog( '103582791475538230', '766312101614724073', '573805391546193767', '28772581', '573805391546415335' );" data-tooltip-text="Report this post for inappropriate content.  Reported post are flagged for review by moderators.">
				<span class="non_breaking_space">&nbsp;</span><img src="https://community.akamai.steamstatic.com/public/images/skin_1/notification_icon_flag_dark.png?v=1">Report this post</a>
			</div>
							</div>
			</div>
			<div class="commentthread_comment_text" id="comment_content_573805391546415335">
				<blockquote class="bb_blockquote with_author"><div class="bb_quoteauthor">Originally posted by <b><a href="#c573805391546342993">LukeFF</a></b>:</div>You can order them to or to not call out enemy contacts from the command menu. </blockquote><br>Which is inconsistent, half the time they *still* don't do it, and anyway should be the default behavior and *not* something I have to check each sortie. In general, as I note above, the AI seems to only ever half reply to your commands which means you really don't know if the command has taken, if the behavior has changed, etc. until after its too late. Poor response to player input.<br><br><blockquote class="bb_blockquote">The Ai behavior is set on automatic by default and act on everything without requiring your flight lead input. This also means that they often won't respond to your commands.<br>If you would rather they obey to your commands, mostly, go to settings/game/artificial intelligence and select the option &quot;Maintain Formation&quot;. I noticed more radio replies when this is turned on, such as flight formation confirmations.</blockquote><br>Thanks I will try this and see if it helps. A voice rework would be very appreciated overall. I've slowly come to 'understand' the AI voice, whenever it does trigger, but its like learning greek it can be very garbled. The Korean voices in my MiG-15 are quite poor, coming from someone whose been trying to learn Korean a few years now. I don't hate what theyre going for with this new voice system, but where it is now is unnecessarily challenging.			</div>
			<div class="comment_footer_ctn">
									<div></div>
				
				
									<div class="forum_comment_permlink">
						<span class="forum_comment_moderate">
													</span>
