			<div class="forum_comment_action_menu" style="display: none;" id="forum_comment_actions_menu_573805391546434653">				<a class="forum_comment_action report tooltip" href="javascript:Forum_ShowReportDialog( '103582791475538230', '766312101614724073', '573805391546193767', '20296525', '573805391546434653' );" data-tooltip-text="Report this post for inappropriate content.  Reported post are flagged for review by moderators.">
				<span class="non_breaking_space">&nbsp;</span><img src="https://community.akamai.steamstatic.com/public/images/skin_1/notification_icon_flag_dark.png?v=1">Report this post</a>
			</div>
							</div>
			</div>
			<div class="commentthread_comment_text" id="comment_content_573805391546434653">
				<blockquote class="bb_blockquote with_author"><div class="bb_quoteauthor">Originally posted by <b><a href="#c573805391546343319">PopaStern</a></b>:</div>The Ai behavior is set on automatic by default and act on everything without requiring your flight lead input. This also means that they often won't respond to your commands.   <br>If you would rather they obey to your commands, mostly, go to settings/game/artificial intelligence and select the option &quot;Maintain Formation&quot;.  I noticed more radio replies when this is turned on, such as flight formation confirmations.<br><br>I also would like having more control on radio volume in the future.<br>My biggest negative on this topic is the often uncomprehensible ai voices forcing me to open my map screen to read the chat bubbles. <br><br>I read that a voice rework is in the works so we can expect things to get better.<br>Fly safe! </blockquote><br>Yes, we are continuing to work on improving the system.<br><br>BTW, you can control the radio volume just like in GB. The only limitation right now is the radio beacon volume is tied to it as well.			</div>
			<div class="comment_footer_ctn">
